// Design 207: inference NEVER guesses. `Vector()` mentions `T` nowhere — no
// argument carries it and no declared slot is in force — so it is the clean
// underdetermined error, naming the parameter and the explicit spelling. The
// defaulted allocator is left out of the hint, since nobody writes it.
// EXPECT: error
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: cannot infer type argument `T` for struct `Vector`
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: e.g. `Vector<T>(...)`

func main() {
    let v = Vector()
    print(v.len())
}
